Hello,

I am struggling to figure out how NicheMapR accounts for the latent heat of fusion and solidification of moisture within the soil/snow. If I am not mistaken, latent heat of fusion/solidification of water (phase change) is a key component for why soil/snow can maintain ~0 C

Anything could help, I noticed that if moisture is present in soil and temps are around 0 C, the latent heat of fusion (333 J/kg) is added to the specific heat computation of soil. But how?

Thank You!

