Hi Nicholas,

The microclimate model assumes the ~2m deep soil temperature is the running mean of the past year of 2m height air temperature records, as a boundary condition. That should be a very good approximation to a cave temperature. But exactly what the temperature and humidity is will depend on how air is flowing through it, presence of water bodies in the cave, etc. It's one of the rare situations where the standard bioclim mean annual temperature is a very good approximation for the temperature experienced by an organism!

All the best,
Mike

